RL Requirements\n- The URL must be a valid HTML documentation webpage from the microsoft.com domain\n- Binary files (PDF, DOCX, images, etc.) are not supported\n\n## Output Format\nmarkdown with headings, code blocks, tables, and links preserved.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"description":"URL of the Microsoft documentation page to read","type":"string"}},"required":["url"]},"name":"microsoft_docs_fetch"}]},{"id":"rs_061e797d8d184367006aa1df453f2887d0a8000443853a135f","type":"reasoning","content":[],"encrypted_content":"","summary":[]},{"id":"mcp_061e797d8d184367006aa1df46283887d0bd8654276ac3ac70","type":"mcp_call","status":"completed","approval_request_id":null,"arguments":"{\"query\":\"Azure OpenAI Service documentation overview quickstart models Microsoft Learn\"}","error":null,"name":"microsoft_docs_search","output":"{\"results\": [{\"title\": \"Intern project using Azure OpenAI - Microsoft Q&A\", \"content\": \"Intern project using Azure OpenAI - Microsoft Q&A Hello, I'm an intern on the Python services team. My project revolves around using the Azure OpenAI service. I was wondering if anyone with expertise using this service could meet with me this week to talk more about its capabilities? Or point me in the right direction to get the help I'm looking for. Thanks!\\n##Accepted Answers:\\nHi\\nAngel Alvarado Reyes\\n\\u2022\\nAzure Open AI documentation is robust and categorized into multiple section\\nMain Categories on the Azure OpenAI Documentation Site\\nOverview\\nIntroduction to Azure OpenAI Service\\nKey capabilities and use cases\\nSupported models (e.g., GPT-4, GPT-3.5, DALL\\u00b7E, Whisper)\\nQuickstarts\\nHow to get started with the service\\nSample apps and setup guides\\nHow-to Guides\\nDeploying models\\nUsing your own data (RAG)\\nPrompt engineering\\nFine-tuning models\\nConcepts\\nModel lifecycle\\nResponsible AI\\nContent filtering\\nAuthentication and authorization\\nTutorials\\nEnd-to-end examples\\nIntegration with other Azure services\\nReference\\nREST API reference\\nSDKs for Python, .NET, Java, JavaScript\\nResources\\nPricing\\nQuotas and limits\\nRegional availability\\nYou can start from\\nQuickstarts section\\nand gradually deep dive into all concepts like assistants, video generation, embedding, api_version etc\\nfrom concepts section.\\nAzure OpenAI documentation\\nFeel free to leverage windows copilot to understand any new concept or procure any sample usage based on documentation.\\nYou can post your queries here on forum if you are facing difficulties while developing any POCs.\\nThank you.\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/answers/a/2060260\"}, {\"title\": \"Quickstart: Speech to text with Azure OpenAI transcription models (rest-api)\", \"content\": \"# Quickstart: Speech to text with Azure OpenAI transcription models (rest-api)\\nIn this quickstart, you transcribe speech to text by using the [OpenAI transcription model](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/speech-service/transcribe-overview). The transcription model can transcribe human speech in numerous languages and translate other languages into English.\\nFor offline transcription, use `gpt-transcribe`. This model uses the Audio API transcription path and isn't a Realtime API model.\\nThis quickstart uses a file upload request and response flow (one request per audio file), not a live streaming session.\\nFor offline transcription, use `gpt-transcribe`. This model uses the Audio API transcription path and isn't a Realtime API model.\\nThis quickstart uses a file upload request and response flow (one request per audio file), not a live streaming session.\\nTip\\nThis quickstart takes approximately 10-15 minutes to complete.\\n## Prerequisites\\n1. An Azure subscription - [Create one for free](https://azure.microsoft.com/pricing/purchase-options/azure-account?cid=msft_learn).\\n2. An Azure OpenAI resource with a speech to text model deployed in a [supported region](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/foundry-models/concepts/models-sold-directly-by-azure?tabs=standard-audio). For more information, see [Create a resource and deploy a model with Azure OpenAI](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry-classic/openai/how-to/create-resource).\\n3. Be sure that you are assigned at least the [Cognitive Services Contributor](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry-classic/openai/how-to/role-based-access-control#cognitive-services-contributor) role for the Azure OpenAI resource.\\n4. A sample audio file. You can get sample audio, such as *wikipediaOcelot.wav*, from the [Azure Speech in Foundry Tools SDK repository at GitHub](https://github.com/Azure-Samples/cognitive-services-speech-sdk/tree/master/sampledata/audiofiles).\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/openai/whisper-quickstart\"}, {\"title\": \"Quickstart: Speech to text with Azure OpenAI transcription models (programming-language-powershell)\", \"content\": \"# Quickstart: Speech to text with Azure OpenAI transcription models (programming-language-powershell)\\nIn this quickstart, you transcribe speech to text by using the [OpenAI transcription model](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/speech-service/transcribe-overview). The transcription model can transcribe human speech in numerous languages and translate other languages into English.\\nFor offline transcription, use `gpt-transcribe`. This model uses the Audio API transcription path and isn't a Realtime API model.\\nThis quickstart uses a file upload request and response flow (one request per audio file), not a live streaming session.\\nFor offline transcription, use `gpt-transcribe`. This model uses the Audio API transcription path and isn't a Realtime API model.\\nThis quickstart uses a file upload request and response flow (one request per audio file), not a live streaming session.\\nTip\\nThis quickstart takes approximately 10-15 minutes to complete.\\n## Prerequisites\\n1. An Azure subscription - [Create one for free](https://azure.microsoft.com/pricing/purchase-options/azure-account?cid=msft_learn)\\n2. [You can use either the latest version, PowerShell 7, or Windows PowerShell 5.1.](https://aka.ms/installpowershell)\\n3. An Azure OpenAI resource with a speech to text model deployed in a [supported region](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/foundry-models/concepts/models-sold-directly-by-azure?tabs=standard-audio). For more information, see [Create a resource and deploy a model with Azure OpenAI](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry-classic/openai/how-to/create-resource).\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/openai/whisper-quickstart\"}, {\"title\": \"Quickstart: Get started generating text using the legacy completions API (programming-language-csharp)\", \"content\": \"# Quickstart: Get started generating text using the legacy completions API (programming-language-csharp)\\n## Clean up resources\\nIf you want to clean up and remove an Azure OpenAI resource, you can delete the resource. Before deleting the resource you must first delete any deployed models.\\n1. [Azure portal](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/multi-service-resource?pivots=azportal#clean-up-resources)\\n2. [Azure CLI](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-services/multi-service-resource?pivots=azcli#clean-up-resources)\\n# Quickstart: Get started generating text using the legacy completions API (programming-language-go)\\nUse this article to get started making your first calls to Azure OpenAI.\\n[Source code](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/tree/main/sdk/ai/azopenai) | [Package (Go)](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/sdk/ai/azopenai)| [Samples](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/sdk/ai/azopenai#pkg-examples)\\n## Prerequisites\\n1. An Azure subscription - [Create one for free](https://azure.microsoft.com/free/cognitive-services?azure-portal=true)\\n2. [Go 1.21.0](https://go.dev/dl/) or higher installed locally.\\n3. An Azure OpenAI in Azure AI Foundry Models resource with the `gpt-35-turbo-instuct` model deployed. For more information about model deployment, see the [resource deployment guide](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/openai/how-to/create-resource).\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/openai/quickstart#clean-up-resources\"}, {\"title\": \"Quickstart: Chat with Azure OpenAI models using your own data (ai-foundry-portal)\", \"content\": \"# Quickstart: Chat with Azure OpenAI models using your own data (ai-foundry-portal)\\n## Clean up resources\\nIf you want to clean up and remove an Azure OpenAI or Azure AI Search resource, you can delete the resource or resource group. Deleting the resource group also deletes any other resources associated with it.\\n1. [Azure AI Search resources](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/search/search-get-started-portal#clean-up-resources)\\n2. [Azure app service resources](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/quickstart-dotnetcore?pivots=development-environment-vs#clean-up-resources)\\n# Quickstart: Chat with Azure OpenAI models using your own data (programming-language-csharp)\\nIn this quickstart, you can use your own data with Azure OpenAI models. Using Azure OpenAI's models on your data can provide you with a powerful conversational AI platform that enables faster and more accurate communication.\\n## Prerequisites\\nThe following resources:\\n1. An Azure subscription - [Create one for free](https://azure.microsoft.com/free/cognitive-services).\\n2. Download the example data from [GitHub](https://github.com/Azure-Samples/cognitive-services-sample-data-files/blob/master/openai/contoso_benefits_document_example.pdf) if you don't have your own data.\\n3. The [.NET 8 SDK](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet/8.0)\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/openai/use-your-data-quickstart#clean-up-resources\"}, {\"title\": \"Quickstart: Get started using chat completions with Azure OpenAI in Azure AI Foundry Models (programming-language-typescript)\", \"content\": \"# Quickstart: Get started using chat completions with Azure OpenAI in Azure AI Foundry Models (programming-language-typescript)\\nUse this article to get started using Azure OpenAI.\\n[Source code](https://github.com/openai/openai-node) | [Package (npm)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/openai) | [Samples](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-js/tree/main/sdk/openai/openai/samples)\\nNote\\nThis guide uses the [latest OpenAI npm package](https://www.npmjs.com/package/openai) which now fully supports Azure OpenAI. If you're looking for code examples for the legacy Azure OpenAI JavaScript SDK, they're currently still [available in this repo](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-js/tree/main/sdk/openai/openai/samples/v2-beta/javascript).\\n## Prerequisites\\n1. An Azure subscription - [Create one for free](https://azure.microsoft.com/free/cognitive-services?azure-portal=true)\\n2. [LTS versions of Node.js](https://github.com/nodejs/release#release-schedule)\\n3. [TypeScript](https://www.typescriptlang.org/download/)\\n4. [Azure CLI](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/install-azure-cli) used for passwordless authentication in a local development environment, create the necessary context by signing in with the Azure CLI.\\n5. An Azure OpenAI in Azure AI Foundry Models resource with a `gpt-4` series model deployed. For more information about model deployment, see the [resource deployment guide](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/openai/how-to/create-resource).\\n### Microsoft Entra ID prerequisites\\nFor the recommended keyless authentication with Microsoft Entra ID, you need to:\\n1. Install the [Azure CLI](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/install-azure-cli) used for keyless authentication with Microsoft Entra ID.\\n2. Assign the `Cognitive Services User` role to your user account. You can assign roles 