ou need to:\\n1. Install the [Azure CLI](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cli/azure/install-azure-cli) used for keyless authentication with Microsoft Entra ID.\\n2. Assign the `Cognitive Services User` role to your user account. You can assign roles in the Azure portal under **Access control (IAM)** > **Add role assignment**.\\n### Set up\\n1. Create a new folder `image-quickstart` and go to the quickstart folder with the following command:\\n```shell\\n mkdir image-quickstart && cd image-quickstart\\n```\\n2. Create a new console application with the following command:\\n```shell\\n dotnet new console\\n```\\n3. Install the [OpenAI .NET client library](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Azure.AI.OpenAI/) with the [dotnet add package](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/tools/dotnet-add-package) command:\\n```console\\n dotnet add package Azure.AI.OpenAI --version 1.0.0-beta.6\\n```\\n4. For the **recommended** keyless authentication with Microsoft Entra ID, install the [Azure.Identity](https://www.nuget.org/packages/Azure.Identity) package with:\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/openai/how-to/dall-e#quickstart\"}, {\"title\": \"Quickstart: Get started generating text using the legacy completions API (programming-language-studio)\", \"content\": \"# Quickstart: Get started generating text using the legacy completions API (programming-language-studio)\\nUse this article to get started making your first calls to Azure OpenAI.\\n## Prerequisites\\n1. An Azure subscription - [Create one for free](https://azure.microsoft.com/free/cognitive-services).\\n2. An Azure OpenAI resource with a model deployed. For more information about model deployment, see the [resource deployment guide](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/openai/how-to/create-resource).\\n## Go to the Azure AI Foundry\\nNavigate to the [Azure AI Foundry portal](https://ai.azure.com/) and sign-in with credentials that have access to your Azure OpenAI resource. Durin